---Does the incoming JWT qualify?
---
---All populated fields must pass; omitted fields are skipped. At least one
---of `subject_prefix` (other than a wildcard-only value like `*`), `claims`,
---or `condition` is required; `audience` alone is not sufficient.
---@class anthropic.organizations.RuleMatch
---@field audience? string|distilled.Null Exact match against the `aud` claim (any element if array). When omitted, the JWT's `aud` must still equal Anthropic's expected audience for the issuer; setting this field overrides that default.
---@field claims? anthropic.organizations.RuleMatchClaimsMap|distilled.Null Exact-match `{claim: value}` pairs against top-level claims. Only string-valued claims can be matched; use `condition` for non-string claims.
---@field condition? string|distilled.Null CEL expression over claims for logic the structural fields can't express. Must evaluate to a boolean and may reference only the `claims` variable; a constant-true expression (such as `true`) is rejected with 400.
---@field subject_prefix? string|distilled.Null Match the verified JWT `sub` claim. Exact match unless the value ends with `*`, in which case it is a prefix match. Example: `repo:my-org/my-repo:ref:refs/heads/main`.

---@alias anthropic.organizations.RuleMatchClaimsMap { [string]: string }

